## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of low-level memory management, per-thread caching strategies, lock-free data structures, memory ordering semantics, and NUMA awareness in practical allocator design.

## Key Concepts
- Fixed-size block allocators
- Thread-local storage (TLS) freelists with global slab pool
- Lock-free freelist with ABA avoidance using atomic compare-exchange
- Memory ordering: acquire/release semantics
- NUMA locality considerations and fragmentation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: alloc/free for fixed-size blocks
typedef struct Block { struct Block* next; } Block;
Block* tls_freelist_head;
Block* global_pool_pull();

Block* alloc() {
  Block* b = tls_freelist_head;
  if (!b) {
    b = global_pool_pull();
    if (!b) return NULL; // OOM
  }
  tls_freelist_head = b->next;
  return b;
}

void free(Block* b) {
  b->next = tls_freelist_head;
  tls_freelist_head = b;
}
```
